 ## Overview
-Slice Filling with BFS Propagation extends simple slice filling by propagating filled voxels to adjacent neighbors within the same 2D slice plane using a Breadth-First Search (BFS) [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently marking empty space in a voxel grid while respecting solid boundaries, ensuring that connectivity is maintained across the slice [S1, unofficial]. It is distinguished from its sibling [Slice Filling (Simple)](1691-slice-filling-simple.md) by using BFS propagation to fill contiguous empty regions rather than scanning linearly from both ends [S1, unofficial].
+Slice Filling with BFS Propagation extends simple slice filling by propagating filled voxels to adjacent neighbors within the same 2D slice plane using a Breadth-First Search (BFS) if the neighbor is also empty in both the main voxel grid and the current buffer [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently marking empty space in a voxel grid while respecting solid boundaries, ensuring connectivity is maintained across the slice [S1, unofficial]. It is distinguished from its sibling [Slice Filling (Simple)](1691-slice-filling-simple.md) by using BFS propagation to fill contiguous empty regions rather than scanning linearly from both ends [S1, unofficial].
 
